{
  "$comment": [
    "AES-CCM known-answer vectors, verbatim from RFC 3610 'Counter with CBC-MAC (CCM)',",
    "appendix A. Extracted programmatically from the RFC text rather than transcribed by",
    "hand, because a transcription error in a crypto vector produces a test that passes",
    "for the wrong reason.",
    "",
    "These validate the vendored tinycrypt primitive (decision D4) against a published",
    "source rather than against tinycrypt's own copy of the same vectors. That is what",
    "docs/test-plan.md gate 2.15 asks for: 'matches published AES-CCM test vectors'.",
    "",
    "All 24 use a 13-byte nonce, which is what CLAUDE.md 2.1 specifies and what tinycrypt",
    "requires. The tag lengths here are 8 and 10 bytes; the frame format uses 4, which RFC",
    "3610 does not cover -- that construction is pinned separately by a regression fixture",
    "in firmware/test/unit/test_crypto.cpp."
  ],
  "spec": "RFC 3610 appendix A",
  "source": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3610.txt",
  "count": 24,
